  "body": "We've had to build debs twice over the past two days, and each time `debian:stretch` is failing with obscure logs ([see here](https://vector.modular.im/_matrix/media/r0/download/vector.modular.im/6dd8279e0f6776416cd7040d56eb43159e2418a2)) and succeeding when rerun.\r\n\r\nOn top of that, today, the `ubuntu:bionic` one failed with a different but also strange error ([see here](https://vector.modular.im/_matrix/media/r0/download/vector.modular.im/6753ff9c414be4165c66afe02067d9abe3d21855)).\r\n\r\nFWIW I've only seen it fail when running the builds concurrently (`-jX`) but then I've been running that mode for 3/4 of my attempts so cases where I haven't ran it in that mode are clearly a minority and might not be of any significance.",
